            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="1051" n="935" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg935"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51 Et 3/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-09T12:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                                1923—12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 11:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Department’s 17, November 6, 3 p.m. Department’s information essentially
                    correct. Full text mailed October 30th. Information <pb facs="1052" n="936"
                        xml:id="pg936"/> here indicates final contract may not be signed. Strong
                    opposition. President still in Guayaquil. Will keep Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bading</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
